    "summary": "Stellar Lovelight duet with Janis & Pigpen plus tight Not Fade Away jam",
    "blurb": "The show features a historic Janis Joplin guest spot on Turn On Your Lovelight and a soaring Candyman. The second set delivers a blistering Not Fade Away that flows into Saint Stephen, highlighted by crystal‑clear guitar tones and tight band interplay.",
    "review": "On July 16, 1970 at the Euphoria Ballroom, the Dead served up one of the most memorable guest moments in their early years – Janice Joplin joining Ron \"Pigpen\" McKernan and Jerry for an electrifying Turn On Your Lovelight duet that still feels fresh. The first set rides a smooth wave from Me And My Uncle through a classic China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue into the heartfelt Candyman, keeping the energy high throughout. The second set is pure fire: a tight‑knit Not Fade Away blossoms into Saint Stephen with Jerry’s “crystal‑clear” guitar tone soaring, while Bob Weir locks in on rhythm and lead. Attics Of My Life and Cumberland Blues add depth, and the encore of Turn On Your Lovelight* rounds out a night that captures both historic guest magic and the band’s tight early‑70s chemistry.",
